            <ArticleTitle>MR imaging of complications of loose surgical tacks in the shoulder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Loose surgical tacks in the shoulder joint are a potential cause of new-onset shoulder pain after arthroscopic repair of an anterior-to-posterior lesion of the superior labrum. We report the MR imaging appearance of loose surgical tacks in this anatomic location.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">MR imaging is valuable in the evaluation of postoperative shoulder pain. Synovitis is a commonly considered clinical diagnosis; our report illustrates that loose tacks are another potential complication after shoulder surgery</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
